    "https://www.randolphcollege.edu/humanresources/faculty-searches/assistant-professor-of-economics-and-business-2/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and Business",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Economics and Business - Faculty Searches - Human Resources - Randolph College Randolph College Home Page Give Today! Support Randolph College APPLY REQUEST VISIT NEWS A-Z ALUMNAE & ALUMNI PARENTS & FAMILIES INSIDE RANDOLPH Search the Randolph Web Site About Admission Undergraduate Graduate Academics Undergraduate Graduate Student Life Athletics Outcomes Alumnae & Alumni Parents & Families Inside Randolph APPLY REQUEST VISIT NEWS EVENTS Support Randolph Search ABOUT ADMISSION Undergraduate Graduate ACADEMICS Undergraduate Graduate STUDENT LIFE ATHLETICS OUTCOMES ABOUT ADMISSION Undergraduate Graduate ACADEMICS Undergraduate Graduate STUDENT LIFE ATHLETICS OUTCOMES Human Resources Home Job Openings Faculty Searches Staff Non-Discrimination and Equal Employment Opportunity Resources for Faculty and Staff Benefits Payroll Dates Holidays Wellness Employee Handbook New Employee Information Organizational Chart Forms & Policies Student Employment Student Job Listings Links Princeton Review Top 25 Green Colleges Randolph College is ranked among the Top 40 Green Colleges by The Princeton Review October 15, 2026 Assistant Professor of Economics and Business Salary Range: $72,000 – $80,000 The Department of Economics and Business at Randolph College invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor. The ability to teach principles of macroeconomics, intermediate macroeconomics, the economics senior capstone course and senior paper, and related electives is required. Electives that would enhance our curriculum include international economics and money and banking. The successful applicant must be committed to excellent undergraduate teaching in the liberal arts tradition. The position carries a 3-3 teaching load. Date of employment is July 1, 2027; report date is in mid-August. Applicants will receive priority consideration if a) their application package is received by November 16, 2026, and b) a Ph.D. is expected by September 1, 2027. To apply, please send the following materials to econsearch@randolphcollege.edu (1) a letter of interest in Randolph College, (2) CV, (3) teaching evaluations, (4) a philosophy of teaching statement, (5) graduate transcript(s), and (6) three letters of recommendation (one of which must address teaching competence). The cover letter should indicate the range of elective courses you would be willing to teach. Candidates chosen to be interviewed will be contacted by phone. Located in the shadow of the Blue Ridge Mountains in Lynchburg, Virginia, Randolph College, founded in 1891 as Randolph-Macon Woman’s College, is a traditional small liberal arts college with a longstanding reputation for excellence in teaching and an appreciation for and commitment to inclusivity. Randolph College is notable for its innovative curricular model, TAKE2.  Students enroll in coursework over four 7-week sessions in an academic year, allowing them to sharpen their focus with immersive learning, gain life balance with a more flexible schedule, and thrive within a supportive, student-centered environment. Randolph is an EOE M/F/D/V employer. << previous post Randolph College is a private liberal arts college in Lynchburg, Virginia attracting students from Virginia, Maryland, North Carolina, and beyond. We provide a rigorous academic program that features small classes with top-ranked professors and hands-on, experiential learning. Employment Application Download PDF View Current Job Openings 2500 RIVERMONT AVE. LYNCHBURG, VA 24503 434-947-8000 CONTACT US RESOURCES FAST FACTS EMERGENCY INFO DISCLOSURE PRIVACY POLICY TITLE IX ON CAMPUS CALENDAR MAPS & DIRECTIONS CAMPUS STORE MAIER MUSEUM OF ART ENDSTATION THEATRE POPULAR LINKS A-Z INDEX PRESIDENT FINANCIAL AID EMPLOYMENT GRADUATE DEGREES FOLLOW US REQUEST ADMISSION INFO SCHEDULE A VISIT APPLY NOW GIVE TODAY"
